  "constraints": {
    "notes": "BF16 float ports are 2-byte aligned; counts/spans and FP32 scratch are 4-byte aligned. All *_elements and *_stride counts use the pointed-to dtype, not bytes. Reject BF16 rounding overflow before publishing any output. Checked capacities, strides, alignment, finite operands/results and disjoint writable regions. Rejection leaves every gradient output unchanged; scratch unspecified. Overwrite valid gradients, do not accumulate prior calls. Nondifferentiable spans/counts. No allocations. Recompute forward FP32 probabilities using ordered FP64 reductions. dProbability dot and weighted mean use FP64, dProbability and scaled dLogit stored FP32. Direct/value and score paths use separate FP32 products then FP32 sum; field gradients sum FP64 ascending options. Both output gradients publish atomically."
