  "notes": "BF16-storage VJP: exactly expand BF16 operands, execute the existing FP32-compute VJP, RNE-round gradients to BF16. No intermediate BF16 rounding inside the VJP. This is not parity with arbitrary PyTorch BF16/autocast forward graphs, full BF16 head training, or a speed claim. Generated VJP building block; not automatic head-backward synthesis or full trainer certification. Recompute forward FP32 probabilities using ordered FP64 reductions. dProbability dot and weighted mean use FP64, dProbability and scaled dLogit stored FP32. Direct/value and score paths use separate FP32 products then FP32 sum; field gradients sum FP64 ascending options. Both output gradients publish atomically."
